ved_at of 23:42:10 and its implied 6.9-minute (415-second) wait cannot be reconciled with the trace. Two admitted artifacts therefore contradict each other directly on arrival and dwell, and no clause resolves the conflict.\n\nOn the parties' competing claims: the rider's case that the 6.9-minute window (415 seconds, from the arrival tap to cancellation) falls 65 seconds short reads the tap, but POL-NS-01(c) measures the dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, and once the skew is allowed for the same trace yields 632 seconds, so the shortfall is not proved. The driver's case that the corrected 632 seconds puts him over the minimum is equally unprovable, because the 186-second gap hides the entry moment. The accumulated-dwell route under POL-NS-06(i) is unavailable: EV-ADVIS-00210-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0, and the limb requires a present, populated advisory. On POL-NS-02 the driver's closest approach of 96 m is inside the 150 m AIRPORT radius with 5 qualifying fixes, so proximity is met on the face of the trace, but that only turns the dispute to dwell, which is undecided.\n\nThe driver's compensation claim under POL-NS-07 (SGD 4.80, being 80 percent of the SGD 6.00 fee) fails because POL-NS-07 requires POL-NS-01 satisfied in full, which it is not. The anti-farming check does not trip - no_show_terminations_30d of 2 is below 4 and 2/156 = 0.013 is below 0.08 - so no abuse finding and no packet from that branch. On the rider's exoneration routes: POL-NS-04 does not apply, because the only surviving rider message ('why cancel?? i was at door 6') was sent at 23:49:40, after the 23:49:05 cancellation, so limb (a) fails, and limb (c) is undecidable because the trace carries no rider_track (PARTIAL_RECORD), which is neutral rather than adverse. POL-NS-05 cannot be run at all while the 228-second skew makes the arrival marker unmatchable, so no false-arrival finding is entered. POL-NS-03 is not engaged, the driver's fixes sitting inside the 150 m radius.\n\nConfidence is capped at 0.25, the weight of the sole artifact (the GPS trace) that carries the dwell under POL-NS-01(c), far below the 0.70 floor. Escalation is triggered three ways: POL-NS-09(b) (two admitted artifacts contradict on arrival and dwell, unresolved by any clause), POL-NS-09(e) (the sole evidence for the deciding fact is impaired under POL-NS-08(a) and (b)), and POL-NS-09(a) (confidence below the floor). No referral is issued: POL-NS-05(ii) cannot fire because the clause cannot be run, and POL-NS-07's anti-farming branch has not tripped. The open question for the reviewer is when the driver actually entered the geofence - whether the 228-second device skew should be corrected (632 seconds, fee chargeable) or not (404 seconds, fee refundable) - and whether the 186-second gap conceals an entry before 23:42:10."
