{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.25,
    "explanation": "I cannot resolve this dispute on the record, so I am escalating it rather than ruling for either of you. The SGD 6.00 fee is placed on hold: it is not collected from the rider and not refunded, and no compensation is paid to the driver, until a human reviewer settles the single fact that decides the case — when the driver's car actually entered the Door 6 geofence at Changi T1. I record that this is not an abuse finding against either party: the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 2, below the threshold of 4, and 2/156 = 0.013, below the 0.08 rate limb), rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1, and both counterparty-dispute counters are 0, so POL-NS-09(c) and (d) are not engaged.\n\nWhat IS settled. The fee itself is correctly raised: EV-FARE-00210 is COMPLETE at weight 1.0, and its SGD 6.00 cancellation-fee line equals the greater of the AIRPORT zone-class fee (SGD 6.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00), so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged. payment_status is PENDING and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00, so nothing has moved yet. The driver's POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (d) are also made out — the trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event and a driver termination at 23:49:05 under RIDER_NO_SHOW — and his trace does place him inside the 150 m AIRPORT arrival radius (closest approach 96.0 m, 5 qualifying in-geofence fixes), so this is not a wrong-face-of-venue case under POL-NS-03.\n\nWhat is NOT settled is POL-NS-01 limb (c): a continuous in-geofence dwell of at least 480 seconds, measured from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix and not from the 'arrived' tap. That measurement cannot safely be made. EV-GPS-00210 is impaired under POL-NS-08(a) and (b): the driver-device clock runs 228 seconds ahead of the server (far over the 90-second limb), a 186-second sampling gap sits exactly across the moment of geofence entry, coverage is 22.8%, the trace stops 149 seconds before the cancellation, and rider_track is absent. It is also the only evidence of the dwell. Read at face value the first in-geofence fix is 23:42:21 and the dwell to the 23:49:05 cancellation is 404 seconds — 76 seconds short of 480. Corrected for the 228-second skew the same fix is 23:38:33 server time and the dwell is 632 seconds — comfortably over. The 186-second gap conceals which reading is right, and no clause resolves it.\n\nRider: your shortfall case (the trip record's 6.9-minute wait, or 415 seconds from arrived_at to cancelled_at) does not decide limb (c), because the clause measures the dwell from the first qualifying GPS fix, not from the arrival tap, and EV-TRIP-00210 is itself impaired at weight 0.4 (CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT) and cannot carry the point. A full refund under POL-NS-06 would need the shortfall established; it is not. Driver: the mirror argument fails for the same reason — the very skew and gap you rely on to lengthen the dwell to 632 seconds are what make it unverifiable, and POL-NS-07 compensation of SGD 4.80 cannot be paid on an unsatisfied limb (c), so I reject that claim. Rider: your POL-NS-04 exoneration route also fails on its own terms — your only surviving message ('why cancel?? i was at door 6') was sent at 23:49:40, 35 seconds after the cancellation, so limb (a) cannot be run, and limb (c) is undecidable because the trace carries no rider_track; the chat log's truncation (weight 0.6, TRUNCATED_LOG) does not help either side.\n\nSo the case escalates under POL-NS-09(b), (e) and (a): two admissible artifacts contradict each other directly on arrival and dwell and no clause resolves the conflict; the sole evidence for the deciding fact is impaired under POL-NS-08(a)–(b); and the deciding artifact weighs 0.25, below the 0.70 floor, which caps my confidence at 0.25. The open question the reviewer must settle is: on a corrected clock, when did the driver enter the Door 6 geofence, and did his continuous in-geofence dwell reach 480 seconds before he cancelled at 23:4